{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Driven.</b> Like the form of 'driven' in haste." "<b>And the city of Shushan.</b> For there the Jews were bewildered. But why should the capital care, for all of it is servants of the king, and there is no Jew there except Mordecai alone." "<b>Bewildered.</b> A past-tense verb, therefore it is mil'el, from the root of נְבוּכִים (the bewildered). 'They are in the land' — like a man who is confounded and does not know what to do. And Mordecai, as soon as he knew this thing, immediately rent his garments."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:56.278308459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}